1
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:09,777
The world.

2
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:11,797
What a glorious place.

3
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:16,097
Seek freedom, and it will lie
stretched out before your eyes.

4
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:19,320
If the endless dream guides
your restless spirit,

5
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:23,960
seize it, raise your flag, and stand tall.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,697
I think back to the time
when my search first began.

7
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:35,337
I left behind those shores of sand.

8
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:38,600
For the endless everlasting
world out there.

9
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:42,817
I know that with this
burning passion driving me.

10
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:48,580
Someday, somewhere, I'll finally see the
light I have searched for everywhere?.

11
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:55,737
When the summer sun is shining.

12
00:00:55,820 --> 00:00:58,677
Shaking the sails of my heart. But I know.

13
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:04,417
A brand new world

14
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:05,817
that has been hiding.

15
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:08,937
Has opened up its doors for me to go.

16
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:11,880
A great long blue sky.

17
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:15,357
Weighing in the troubled waves.

18
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:17,857
From all despair I can be saved.

19
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:21,197
For the horizon on the other side is.

20
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:23,537
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

21
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:25,577
Is what I am for.

22
00:01:25,660 --> 00:01:28,557
And though I've traveled far
from where my search began.

23
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:31,197
Overseas of green and shores of sand.

24
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:34,560
Through the endless
everlasting world out there.

25
00:01:35,380 --> 00:01:38,757
I know that with this
burning passion driving me.

26
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:44,420
Someday somewhere I'll finally see the
light I have searched for everywhere.

27
00:01:57,060 --> 00:01:57,890
Captain!

28
00:01:58,120 --> 00:01:58,950
Captain!

29
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:06,760
One tooth is the size of our
boat! That's it! We're dead!

30
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:08,157
There's no monster!

31
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:11,877
This is just one big stupid dream that
we're all having together for some reason!

32
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:12,920
A dream, right!

33
00:02:13,740 --> 00:02:15,340
It was just a dream!

34
00:02:16,060 --> 00:02:17,140
You know...

35
00:02:18,620 --> 00:02:20,180
Our boys just got eaten.

36
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:27,037
So did that ship we
were trying to salvage.

37
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:28,600
How can you be so calm?

38
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:34,548
Yep, most definitely eaten.

39
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:36,857
I can see the air hoses
dangling from its jaws.

40
00:02:36,940 --> 00:02:37,770
Stop.

41
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:46,100
I can't stop.

42
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:48,017
I see my hair and my friends.

43
00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:49,394
What am I going to do?

44
00:02:51,620 --> 00:02:52,973
This is all your fault!

45
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:55,757
You're the one who said it would be
safe at the bottom of the Grand Line.

46
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:58,097
I don't know what qualifies
as safe in your book,

47
00:02:58,180 --> 00:03:00,592
but in mine, it's not man-eating turtles!

48
00:03:01,940 --> 00:03:02,770
You're right.

49
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:06,030
Sorry!

50
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:09,813
It's as good as it's gonna get, I guess.

51
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:23,937
If we don't cut the air hoses that beast

52
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:25,997
will drag us down to
the bottom of the ocean?

53
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:30,237
I don't care what you do just do
something you're the tough and

54
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:34,438
smart lady give me a minute I'll see
I'll see what I can come up with.

55
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:37,240
Okay, boys!

56
00:03:37,580 --> 00:03:39,600
Time to save our noble captain!

57
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:43,200
Our pride, honor, and lives are at stake!

58
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:47,457
Our captain is alive and we will find him!

59
00:03:47,540 --> 00:03:48,370
Mark my words!

60
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:49,910
They're right.

61
00:03:49,993 --> 00:03:54,215
It's these challenging times that
prove the streak by which we are made.

62
00:03:55,760 --> 00:03:56,590
Usopp! Yeah?

63
00:03:57,780 --> 00:04:00,360
Cut the air hoses and get us out of here!

64
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:02,108
This is what we're made of!

65
00:04:06,620 --> 00:04:07,657
What is that?

66
00:04:07,740 --> 00:04:09,600
It's like everything got dark.

67
00:04:14,060 --> 00:04:15,117
There's no way.

68
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:16,557
Why is it so dark?

69
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:17,758
It's not that late.

70
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:21,100
It's time to leave, guys! Now!

71
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,800
Luffy, Zoro, Sanji.

72
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:26,597
This is a bad omen.

73
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:31,197
We all know the suddenly darkened sun is
the harbinger of the monsters to soon rise.

74
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:34,398
Guys, we've got to save the
boss and get out of here!

75
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:39,670
Reef!

76
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:42,857
Tell me what happened!

77
00:04:42,940 --> 00:04:43,770
Are you dead?

78
00:04:43,853 --> 00:04:44,695
Where are the others?

79
00:04:47,420 --> 00:04:49,160
Zoro! Sanji! Set sail now.

80
00:04:49,380 --> 00:04:50,537
We've got to get out of here.

81
00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:51,973
Yeah, that guy's crazy.

82
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:54,077
I'm so glad you're okay.

83
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:57,077
Now let's get away from the
stinky turtle as fast as we can!

84
00:04:57,160 --> 00:04:59,077
No, it wasn't a turtle, it was a monkey!

85
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:01,300
Yeah, bonafide sea monkey.

86
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:05,617
Can't say I'm too surprised that he and
Luffy got along as well as they did.

87
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:07,117
Well, they're both monkeys.

88
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:09,937
But when he caught a glimpse of all the
stuff that we had taken from his ship,

89
00:05:10,020 --> 00:05:12,297
he totally flipped out
and went on a rampage.

90
00:05:12,380 --> 00:05:15,037
I've never seen a primate
act like that before.

91
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:17,677
Yeah, that's Mashida, the
king of all salvagers.

92
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:21,777
But never mind him, how did the three
of you escape from the giant sea turtle?

93
00:05:21,860 --> 00:05:24,448
Ugh, why do you keep
talking about a turtle?

94
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:26,340
Hmm, that's weird.

95
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:29,817
Now he's just floating there like a
statue with his mouth gaping open.

96
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:31,400
Oh, I get it, of course!

97
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:33,217
That's how you guys escaped!

98
00:05:33,300 --> 00:05:35,065
We were in that thing's mouth!

99
00:05:35,360 --> 00:05:37,357
Nothing gets past you guys, does it?

100
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:40,499
That's the turtle that ate
the ship you were inside!

101
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:46,537
Hey, when did night happen?

102
00:05:46,620 --> 00:05:47,920
Attention all hands!

103
00:05:48,140 --> 00:05:49,905
We're getting out of here now!

104
00:05:55,580 --> 00:05:56,410
Ah!

105
00:05:56,493 --> 00:05:57,480
Not so fast!

106
00:05:57,700 --> 00:05:59,641
Hand over the treasure you stole!

107
00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:02,975
Or I'll tear your ship apart
and find all of it anyway!

108
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:04,630
Is he right?

109
00:06:04,713 --> 00:06:05,877
You guys found some treasure?

110
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:07,820
We sure did! Tons of it!

111
00:06:08,340 --> 00:06:09,400
This isn't good.

112
00:06:09,620 --> 00:06:12,385
If he starts rampaging
the ship we all go down.

113
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,277
Hey, Captain!

114
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:18,380
Behind you!

115
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:20,920
What's behind me?

116
00:06:42,180 --> 00:06:45,200
I don't know.

117
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:19,000
Sea Monsters!

118
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:48,866
That couldn't have been real.

119
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:53,820
Those things were taller than the sky.

120
00:07:57,640 --> 00:08:01,077
The Grand Line is an endless
parade of mysteries and annoyance.

121
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:03,777
I mean, look at the nightmare
of just making it through today!

122
00:08:03,860 --> 00:08:07,357
First there was that huge galleon that
fell from the clouds on top of us.

123
00:08:07,440 --> 00:08:10,457
The Log Pose's needle
started pointing to the sky.

124
00:08:10,540 --> 00:08:14,217
A psycho makeup wearing monkey
shows up and blocks our way.

125
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:18,397
And then a gigantic sea turtle
came and ate our salvage ship.

126
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:20,100
Then darkness fell.

127
00:08:20,860 --> 00:08:25,272
Because the biggest monsters I've ever
seen in my life blocked out the sun!

128
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:28,740
I must admit, even I was
intimidated by those things.

129
00:08:37,060 --> 00:08:40,295
Those monsters were too big
for any of us to take them.

130
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:41,550
Yeah.

131
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:44,581
If I never see them again,
it would be a blessing.

132
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:46,380
Don't sweat it.

133
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:47,461
They're nothing.

134
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:53,329
If I really cut loose, I could have
taught those sea monsters a thing or two.

135
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:54,950
Sure.

136
00:08:55,033 --> 00:08:57,311
I fought ten of those things a while back.

137
00:08:57,560 --> 00:08:58,913
You fought ten of them?

138
00:09:01,060 --> 00:09:02,420
Come on, you guys.

139
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:07,442
Tell me you at least tried to find something
down there that we could actually use.

140
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:10,417
All you brought back was
a bunch of scattered junk.

141
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:13,617
There's not a single clue here
about how to get to Sky Island.

142
00:09:13,700 --> 00:09:15,737
There wasn't anything there, believe me.

143
00:09:15,820 --> 00:09:16,880
We looked. Yep.

144
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:20,697
If there was something else down
there, we would have found it.

145
00:09:20,780 --> 00:09:22,597
The ship was in terrible shape,

146
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:26,033
all jacked up like it had
maybe been attacked and raided.

147
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:29,097
Or perhaps a mutiny had
broken out and they all killed

148
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:32,474
each other in a violent
struggle for power and survival.

149
00:09:45,340 --> 00:09:49,957
Look around boys this is exactly why we
need more information intelligence means the

150
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:51,457
difference between life and death for this

151
00:09:51,540 --> 00:09:53,757
whole crew and if we're
gonna sail to Sky Island

152
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:57,357
then we need more information to stay alive
or whatever happened to that ship could

153
00:09:57,440 --> 00:10:00,077
happen to us too we didn't
brave giant monsters

154
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:01,937
so you could bring back a creepy octopus

155
00:10:02,020 --> 00:10:04,077
some rusty swords, and a broken dish!

156
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:06,513
This is all junk, and you're all idiots!

157
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:10,760
What is that, Luffy?

158
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:13,030
Armor.

159
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:18,000
Whoa, she crushed the armor!

160
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:21,237
Nami, you didn't even notice the
pretty seashells I brought you.

161
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:23,157
Cram your seashells in your shorts.

162
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:25,358
She's so beautiful when she's angry.

163
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:28,689
You should still try
to keep your distance.

164
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,017
Bad day huh?

165
00:10:31,100 --> 00:10:34,477
It's only gonna get worse
working with these guys.

166
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:37,097
We'll never figure out how
that ship sailed to the sky.

167
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:38,897
I'm gonna snap on them any second.

168
00:10:38,980 --> 00:10:40,457
Maybe this will help.

169
00:10:40,540 --> 00:10:42,680
Eternal pose!

170
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:44,330
But how?

171
00:10:44,413 --> 00:10:47,117
Oh, I took it off that
salvager's ship earlier.

172
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:48,320
Just in case.

173
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:55,520
You're the only one I can depend on.

174
00:10:57,280 --> 00:11:00,400
All right, who's up for
an octopus dinner tonight?

175
00:11:01,560 --> 00:11:03,740
That boy has got to learn to relax.

176
00:11:09,560 --> 00:11:11,917
Jaya, this must have been their home port?

177
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,700
Jaya, is that where we're going next?

178
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:17,056
That would be your decision, Captain!

179
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:21,660
All hands on deck!

180
00:11:22,900 --> 00:11:25,120
Set our course to Jaya!

181
00:11:28,420 --> 00:11:32,520
So, uh, any of you know which
direction that might be? Starbird.

182
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:34,740
You heard her, chopper. Right.

183
00:11:35,380 --> 00:11:36,880
Onward to Jaya!

184
00:11:38,980 --> 00:11:40,568
Now, hold up just a minute.

185
00:11:41,340 --> 00:11:44,516
If we head off to this Jaya
place that's so important,

186
00:11:44,760 --> 00:11:47,936
won't the Log Pose's needle
change its position again?

187
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:52,997
Because if that happens, we won't
know which direction Sky Island is.

188
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:53,910
What?

189
00:11:53,993 --> 00:11:55,260
All hands full, stop!

190
00:11:55,620 --> 00:11:57,937
Want to tell me why you're
messing with my head, Nami?

191
00:11:58,020 --> 00:11:58,850
I'm not.

192
00:11:58,933 --> 00:12:01,277
You're the genius who
decided we should go to Jaya.

193
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:02,617
Oh, yeah, that's right.

194
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:05,457
Well, I didn't know it was going to
ruin our plans to get to Skypiea.

195
00:12:05,540 --> 00:12:07,937
It's not my fault you have
the memory of a goldfish.

196
00:12:08,020 --> 00:12:10,917
Think, the log poses always
work that way, hasn't it?

197
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,880
Yeah, guess so. Hey! Listen up!

198
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,437
I have an important announcement to make.

199
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:19,226
Seeing as I'm the captain, I say
we set our course for Skypiea!

200
00:12:19,340 --> 00:12:20,837
How do you propose we get there?

201
00:12:20,920 --> 00:12:23,177
We're gonna have to ask
for some directions.

202
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:25,237
Maybe someone in Jaya will know the way.

203
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:27,380
Very well, Jaya it is. Right!

204
00:12:27,820 --> 00:12:28,980
On to Jaya!

205
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:31,480
You already said that!

206
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:35,577
I doubt that the needle would
change as soon as we get there.

207
00:12:35,660 --> 00:12:39,677
So why don't we pull into port and then
leave before it has a chance to adjust?

208
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:40,677
Sounds good to me.

209
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:42,237
If we're lucky, it'll work.

210
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:44,280
That sounds like a plan to us!

211
00:12:45,100 --> 00:12:48,880
Full sail to Jaya, people,
and this time it's for real!

212
00:12:49,620 --> 00:12:52,440
Now stop stuffing your
faces and get to work!

213
00:12:52,660 --> 00:12:54,837
I wonder what this Jaya place is like.

214
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:56,155
I hope it's relaxing.

215
00:12:56,360 --> 00:12:57,242
Nami, my sweet!

216
00:12:57,400 --> 00:12:58,380
Robin, my dear!

217
00:12:58,620 --> 00:12:59,800
Dinner is served!

218
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:10,517
Looks like that's the last of your cash.

219
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:15,057
But if you wanted to, I'd let you
raise with, say, your clothes?

220
00:13:15,140 --> 00:13:17,357
You're lucky and you don't even know it!

221
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,957
Playing with Roscio, even if
you would have won the hand.

222
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:22,687
Trust me, you would have
lost something else!

223
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:25,600
I suppose that about wraps it up.

224
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:32,800
You cheated this entire hand, didn't you?

225
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:37,017
I never cheat, you're a liar. You lie.

226
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:40,377
I watched every deceitful move you made.

227
00:13:40,460 --> 00:13:44,320
You better watch your mouth
in this place, loser Sargus.

228
00:13:45,420 --> 00:13:46,540
Hey Sargus?

229
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,560
Hmm, what is it?

230
00:13:49,060 --> 00:13:51,117
This guy was cheating just now.

231
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:57,117
You saw the whole thing didn't you you
bet I did every rotten little move!

232
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:59,657
He cheated straight through
I said we do something

233
00:13:59,740 --> 00:14:02,117
about this guy make an example out of him.

234
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:04,612
You have no idea who you're dealing with.

235
00:14:33,020 --> 00:14:34,480
You see anything, Usopp?

236
00:14:35,460 --> 00:14:36,290
Nothing.

237
00:14:36,373 --> 00:14:37,371
Just the sky and the sea.

238
00:14:37,540 --> 00:14:40,377
I thought the Jaya Island wasn't
too far from where we were.

239
00:14:40,460 --> 00:14:41,357
It shouldn't be.

240
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:43,137
And with the weather being so clear,

241
00:14:43,220 --> 00:14:45,957
we should have spotted the
coastline over an hour ago.

242
00:14:46,040 --> 00:14:48,737
I'm going to like Jai if
it's as warm as it is now.

243
00:14:48,820 --> 00:14:51,114
I'm finally getting to work on my team.

244
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:54,740
Spring weather's the best.

245
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:58,524
It looks like the Scales
are enjoying it, too.

246
00:14:59,160 --> 00:14:59,990
Hmm.

247
00:15:08,860 --> 00:15:09,920
They've been shot!

248
00:15:10,840 --> 00:15:12,717
Looks like we'll be eating good tonight!

249
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:14,657
I don't think they could
have been shot, Chopper.

250
00:15:14,740 --> 00:15:16,217
I didn't hear any gunfire.

251
00:15:16,300 --> 00:15:17,300
I found a bullet!

252
00:15:17,460 --> 00:15:20,057
And judging from the trajectory,
it came from that way!

253
00:15:20,140 --> 00:15:23,697
Are you saying the shots came from
an island we can't even see yet?

254
00:15:23,780 --> 00:15:25,368
That's impossible, Chopper!

255
00:15:25,460 --> 00:15:27,636
But I saw it happen with my own eyes!

256
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:30,277
A tuna had a better
chance at killing them.

257
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:32,697
No sniper or gun has that kind of range.

258
00:15:32,780 --> 00:15:35,397
They were probably shot before
and just happen to fall now.

259
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:36,310
Hey, Sanji!

260
00:15:36,700 --> 00:15:38,229
Look, we found our dinner!

261
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:46,670
Poor creature.

262
00:15:46,753 --> 00:15:48,177
He must have suffered.

263
00:15:48,260 --> 00:15:51,319
I wasn't able to get an
instant kill on one of them.

264
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:53,497
But that's what fate held for him.

265
00:15:53,580 --> 00:15:56,417
All the events of his life
destined him to this outcome.

266
00:15:56,500 --> 00:15:57,330
So I can't.

267
00:16:04,340 --> 00:16:05,170
Myself.

268
00:16:05,253 --> 00:16:06,297
Hey jerk.

269
00:16:06,380 --> 00:16:08,197
Do you know who I am?

270
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:09,110
No.

271
00:16:09,193 --> 00:16:10,437
Get lost.

272
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:12,217
I'll tell you.

273
00:16:12,300 --> 00:16:13,397
I'm the greatest.

274
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:14,797
Fighting champion ever.

275
00:16:14,880 --> 00:16:19,857
Is

276
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:23,497
it just me or does this

277
00:16:23,580 --> 00:16:24,717
place look like a resort?

278
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:25,920
It sure does!

279
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:27,320
Hurry up and dock!

280
00:16:27,760 --> 00:16:28,937
It does look promising.

281
00:16:29,020 --> 00:16:31,138
Maybe we can even stay here a while.

282
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:32,690
Hmm?

283
00:16:36,740 --> 00:16:41,057
Either I'm starting to hallucinate or the
harbor over there is full of pirate ships.

284
00:16:41,140 --> 00:16:42,720
Don't be silly, Usopp,

285
00:16:42,820 --> 00:16:46,597
since when can pirates dock their ships
in a harbor without being run out of town?

286
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:47,510
You're right.

287
00:16:47,593 --> 00:16:48,539
It must be a joke.

288
00:16:50,460 --> 00:16:51,290
Someone help!

289
00:16:51,373 --> 00:16:52,237
He's gonna kill me!

290
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:54,377
What the heck's going
on with this crazy town?

291
00:16:54,460 --> 00:16:56,080
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

292
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:58,720
What a pathetic little weakling!

293
00:16:59,020 --> 00:17:00,060
Ha, ha, ha!

294
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:03,337
Oh, Missy, you picked
the wrong guy to beat up.

295
00:17:03,420 --> 00:17:04,596
Look at that emblem.

296
00:17:05,100 --> 00:17:06,720
He's in Rocio's gang.

297
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:08,880
You have heard of Race, right?

298
00:17:09,260 --> 00:17:12,820
You know the executioner whose
bounty is 42 million berries?

299
00:17:13,220 --> 00:17:14,520
The man is psychotic.

300
00:17:14,660 --> 00:17:16,248
You better watch your back.

301
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:18,960
That guy is full of it.

302
00:17:19,180 --> 00:17:21,217
We watched that entire game ourselves.

303
00:17:21,300 --> 00:17:22,130
No one cheated.

304
00:17:22,213 --> 00:17:25,628
I still can't believe he was
able to beat up Race so easily.

305
00:17:26,260 --> 00:17:28,620
Don't you know that's Bellamy? What?

306
00:17:28,900 --> 00:17:29,782
That's Bellamy?

307
00:17:29,940 --> 00:17:32,705
The one with the 55
million bounty on his head?

308
00:17:33,680 --> 00:17:34,510
Captain!

309
00:17:34,593 --> 00:17:35,760
I can't believe it!

310
00:17:35,860 --> 00:17:36,697
Who did this to him?

311
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:37,997
We need to get him to a doctor!

312
00:17:38,080 --> 00:17:38,910
Hurry!

313
00:17:38,993 --> 00:17:39,823
Hang in there, Captain.

314
00:17:39,906 --> 00:17:41,213
We'll get you mixed up.

315
00:17:57,700 --> 00:17:59,818
Now this looks like my kind of town.

316
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:02,335
We'll have no problem fitting in here.

317
00:18:03,180 --> 00:18:04,080
There's no way.

318
00:18:04,480 --> 00:18:07,797
Do you think those two can last an
hour without getting into any trouble?

319
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:12,317
Well, by the looks of this place, I'd
say 15 minutes is a generous assumption.

320
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:13,517
You really think so?

321
00:18:13,600 --> 00:18:15,180
I'd better say... Nami!

322
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:18,660
Luffy! Saru! Wait for me! I'm coming too!

323
00:18:19,740 --> 00:18:20,920
There she goes.

324
00:18:21,580 --> 00:18:22,410
Don't worry.

325
00:18:22,493 --> 00:18:24,677
I'm sure she'll be fine with
those two protecting her.

326
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:26,417
I'm the only one who can protect Nami.

327
00:18:26,500 --> 00:18:27,330
Master D!

328
00:18:27,820 --> 00:18:30,217
Nami will be safe and
sound with Luffy and Zoro.

329
00:18:30,300 --> 00:18:32,877
But if you leave, then what are we
supposed to do if this ship is attacked?

330
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:33,790
Don't leave!

331
00:18:33,873 --> 00:18:34,703
Who's gonna protect us?

332
00:18:34,786 --> 00:18:35,797
Fine, I'll stay behind.

333
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:36,780
Let me go.

334
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:41,017
I guess I'll whip up some tea
and hold down the fort, then.

335
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:42,220
Where did Robin go?

336
00:18:43,520 --> 00:18:44,350
Huh?

337
00:18:44,433 --> 00:18:45,263
I don't know.

338
00:18:45,380 --> 00:18:46,937
Sanji, about that tea...

339
00:18:47,020 --> 00:18:48,020
Make it yourself.

340
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:52,957
I got my tough face on, so
if anybody messes with me...

341
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:53,870
No fighting!

342
00:18:53,953 --> 00:18:54,783
Promise me!

343
00:18:54,980 --> 00:18:56,862
Yeah, yeah, whatever, I promise.

344
00:18:57,380 --> 00:18:59,677
Good, this is serious business, you two.

345
00:18:59,760 --> 00:19:00,590
Good.

346
00:19:00,673 --> 00:19:01,503
Great.

347
00:19:01,586 --> 00:19:02,607
Gee, thanks for the support.

348
00:19:03,340 --> 00:19:06,997
Look, if one of you causes trouble here,
we'll have to get out of this town.

349
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:10,677
And if that happens, then we'll never
know how to get to the Sky Island, right?

350
00:19:10,760 --> 00:19:11,590
Yeah.

351
00:19:12,840 --> 00:19:14,260
Whoa, he's messed up.

352
00:19:14,420 --> 00:19:16,097
Looks like he fell off his horse.

353
00:19:16,180 --> 00:19:17,239
That's gotta hurt.

354
00:19:19,500 --> 00:19:21,206
Looks like he's in pain, too.

355
00:19:21,900 --> 00:19:22,730
No doubt.

356
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:27,280
Hey, sorry to bother you,
but will you help me up?

357
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:30,245
What, are you not in the
mood to help yourself?

358
00:19:30,520 --> 00:19:32,280
Luffy, give me a hand. Sure.

359
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:34,030
Up you go.

360
00:19:34,640 --> 00:19:36,520
Hey, would you look at that?

361
00:19:36,720 --> 00:19:38,120
I'm on my horse again.

362
00:19:38,580 --> 00:19:41,760
I was a sickly child growing
up and never got better.

363
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:44,360
Now let's get out of here stronger.

364
00:19:45,180 --> 00:19:46,220
A horse, too?

365
00:19:46,860 --> 00:19:49,154
We should put them out of their misery.

366
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:51,040
Thanks again, pal.

367
00:19:51,380 --> 00:19:56,197
You know, I don't have enough money for a
reward these days, but care for an apple?

368
00:19:56,280 --> 00:19:57,557
Do you take us for idiots?

369
00:19:57,640 --> 00:19:59,517
We'd never trust food
from someone like you.

370
00:19:59,600 --> 00:20:01,520
Hey, look! Apples! Luffy!

371
00:20:04,540 --> 00:20:06,320
What the? What happened?

372
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:09,617
Some guys took a few apples
from that freak on the horse,

373
00:20:09,700 --> 00:20:12,288
and when they bit it
to them, they exploded!

374
00:20:14,100 --> 00:20:14,930
Oh, no! No!

375
00:20:15,540 --> 00:20:16,800
Luffy spit it out!

376
00:20:16,940 --> 00:20:18,497
Spit out the apple you just ate!

377
00:20:18,580 --> 00:20:20,140
I already swallowed it!

378
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:22,640
What the hell did you do that for?

379
00:20:24,940 --> 00:20:27,400
No worries, the boy isn't hurt.

380
00:20:28,240 --> 00:20:29,180
What happened?

381
00:20:29,500 --> 00:20:31,912
I don't know, but the inside's destroyed!

382
00:20:32,380 --> 00:20:36,720
If you had eaten the bad one, you
would have died on the first bite.

383
00:20:39,800 --> 00:20:40,920
You're lucky.

384
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:44,480
What is all this?

385
00:20:44,740 --> 00:20:46,540
It's Oshio's grave now.

386
00:20:47,780 --> 00:20:49,839
It looks like a war broke out here.

387
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:53,177
Did they fire a cannon into the
middle of town or something?

388
00:20:53,260 --> 00:20:54,090
Who knows?

389
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:56,517
Even the people who were
there and saw what happened

390
00:20:56,600 --> 00:20:59,177
said they couldn't tell
exactly what was going on.

391
00:20:59,260 --> 00:21:01,277
About the only thing
everyone knows for certain

392
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:04,066
is that Bellamy had
something to do with this.

393
00:21:04,220 --> 00:21:05,300
Bellamy the hyena?

394
00:21:05,740 --> 00:21:10,505
I think it's pretty obvious that he's
using the power of one of the devil fruits.

395
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:14,944
What's the deal with this town?

396
00:21:15,180 --> 00:21:16,040
I don't know.

397
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:17,200
Who really cares?

398
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:21,077
You should care, seeing as you
were almost killed for no reason.

399
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:23,437
Well, that was bound to
happen sooner or later.

400
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:24,932
Have you lost your mind?

401
00:21:30,380 --> 00:21:31,210
Ah, great.

402
00:21:31,300 --> 00:21:32,130
Look who's back.

403
00:21:32,213 --> 00:21:34,357
How many victims has he racked up now?

404
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:36,937
It's not like he's a famous
fugitive or anything.

405
00:21:37,020 --> 00:21:38,197
Who do you think he is?

406
00:21:38,280 --> 00:21:40,837
I don't care, and to be
honest, I don't want to know.

407
00:21:40,920 --> 00:21:45,508
If that meathead wants to be the fighting
champion, then go ahead and let him.

408
00:21:46,300 --> 00:21:47,359
Fighting champion?

409
00:21:47,680 --> 00:21:50,033
Hey, don't even think about it, you two!

410
00:21:51,040 --> 00:21:51,870
Damn it.

411
00:21:52,080 --> 00:21:55,962
I'm starting to wonder if we can
find any useful information here.

412
00:21:58,880 --> 00:22:00,120
How about this place?

413
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:02,420
Seems pretty quiet to me.

414
00:22:03,160 --> 00:22:04,760
You can say that again.

415
00:22:05,080 --> 00:22:06,557
This place is gorgeous.

416
00:22:06,640 --> 00:22:11,057
To think such an oasis exists in
the middle of this disgusting town?

417
00:22:11,140 --> 00:22:12,177
It's built above the water.

418
00:22:12,260 --> 00:22:13,977
That's great, but there's no one here!

419
00:22:14,060 --> 00:22:16,648
Although I can smell
that someone's cooking.

420
00:22:18,120 --> 00:22:18,950
Excuse me.

421
00:22:19,800 --> 00:22:23,057
Excuse me, I'm going to have to
ask you all to leave, please!

422
00:22:23,140 --> 00:22:25,777
See, the entire hotel has
been rented out by Mr.

423
00:22:25,860 --> 00:22:27,597
Bellamy and his guests And
he's asked that we tell

424
00:22:27,680 --> 00:22:29,417
other guests like yourselves
to go somewhere else?

425
00:22:29,500 --> 00:22:32,317
So uh you must understand that
I have no say in the matter!

426
00:22:32,400 --> 00:22:35,277
So one man rented out
this entire place? If Mr.

427
00:22:35,360 --> 00:22:37,897
Bellamy sees you here, he'll have
my head removed from my body,

428
00:22:37,980 --> 00:22:39,627
so please leave for my sake.

429
00:22:40,280 --> 00:22:42,162
Come on, I'm sure he won't mind.

430
00:22:42,260 --> 00:22:43,907
Who is this Bellamy, anyway?

431
00:22:44,060 --> 00:22:45,360
What's going on here?

432
00:22:46,080 --> 00:22:49,297
Who are these scumbags, and what
are they doing in our hotel?

433
00:22:49,380 --> 00:22:50,210
Mr.

434
00:22:50,293 --> 00:22:51,123
Sargus, welcome back.

435
00:22:51,206 --> 00:22:52,777
I told them to leave,
but they won't listen.

436
00:22:52,860 --> 00:22:53,757
I really don't care.

437
00:22:53,840 --> 00:22:54,670
Just get rid of them.

438
00:22:54,753 --> 00:22:57,297
We're paying a lot of money to
have this place to ourselves.

439
00:22:57,380 --> 00:22:58,210
She's right.

440
00:22:58,293 --> 00:23:00,497
Now get out of here
before I throw you out.

441
00:23:00,580 --> 00:23:02,797
Hey, guys, would you
mind if I beat him up?

442
00:23:02,880 --> 00:23:03,710
Please don't.

443
00:23:03,793 --> 00:23:04,623
Luffy!

444
00:23:04,706 --> 00:23:05,536
Ha!

445
00:23:05,619 --> 00:23:06,449
You're going to beat me up?

446
00:23:06,540 --> 00:23:08,360
Ha ha ha! Hilarious!

447
00:23:10,040 --> 00:23:13,569
Here, go buy some new rags so
you don't look like an orphan.

448
00:23:13,700 --> 00:23:16,917
Sargus, you're wasting your money by
tossing it to this bunch of losers.

449
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:17,830
Ha!

450
00:23:17,913 --> 00:23:18,743
No kidding!

451
00:23:18,826 --> 00:23:20,657
I should have just flushed
it down along with my lunch.

452
00:23:20,740 --> 00:23:21,975
I'll take free money!

453
00:23:22,580 --> 00:23:23,410
Let's go!

454
00:23:23,493 --> 00:23:24,717
These jerks can't help us!

455
00:23:24,800 --> 00:23:26,820
I can walk on my own, you know!

456
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:32,740
Sargus, Lily, just
leave well enough alone.

457
00:23:33,380 --> 00:23:35,380
Eddie, we've been looking for you.

458
00:23:36,080 --> 00:23:38,140
You know that trash you ran into?

459
00:23:38,420 --> 00:23:41,237
Seems they've been doing
pretty well for themselves.

460
00:23:41,320 --> 00:23:42,150
Look.

461
00:23:42,233 --> 00:23:44,617
Not bad, but nothing
compared to you and Bellamy.

462
00:23:44,700 --> 00:23:45,530
Here.

463
00:23:45,613 --> 00:23:47,537
But for ordinary scum,
they can hold their own.

464
00:23:47,620 --> 00:23:51,637
They still don't stand a chance of
surviving the transition into the new era.

465
00:23:51,720 --> 00:23:52,550
Wow.

466
00:23:52,720 --> 00:23:54,680
His bounty is 30 million.

467
00:23:54,980 --> 00:23:56,500
For such a little puke.

468
00:23:56,800 --> 00:23:59,160
I'm sure Bellamy will want to see this.

469
00:24:00,640 --> 00:24:02,657
Man, that really pisses me off.

470
00:24:02,740 --> 00:24:04,920
That's a shame, because, you know,

471
00:24:05,320 --> 00:24:07,697
Mocktown's economy depends
on pirates throwing money

472
00:24:07,780 --> 00:24:10,257
around to show off power
they may or may not have.

473
00:24:10,340 --> 00:24:13,340
What, so poor pirates aren't
allowed on the island?

474
00:24:13,560 --> 00:24:15,877
Looks like there's no
way of calming you down.

475
00:24:15,960 --> 00:24:17,725
Here, this one's on the house.

476
00:24:18,600 --> 00:24:23,057
Tough guys and degenerates are a clientele
here, so trouble isn't hard to find.

477
00:24:23,140 --> 00:24:25,577
You weren't going to make it in
this town if you let it bother you.

478
00:24:25,660 --> 00:24:28,800
You have to play it safe
when you can. Here you go.

479
00:24:29,520 --> 00:24:31,657
This whole town's a real dump, you know.

480
00:24:31,740 --> 00:24:34,837
Of course, that's how most
level-headed people would think of it.

481
00:24:34,920 --> 00:24:38,697
But unfortunately for you, level-headed
people are rare in these parts.

482
00:24:38,780 --> 00:24:41,257
The wanted posters won't be on
the walls for a couple of days,

483
00:24:41,340 --> 00:24:44,497
so you may want to skip town
sooner rather than later.

484
00:24:44,580 --> 00:24:45,620
A couple days?

485
00:24:45,960 --> 00:24:47,777
That doesn't give us much time.

486
00:24:47,860 --> 00:24:49,097
Now here's a question.

487
00:24:49,180 --> 00:24:50,100
Hey, Bacchi!

488
00:24:51,020 --> 00:24:51,850
Huh?

489
00:24:51,933 --> 00:24:52,763
What's wrong?

490
00:24:52,846 --> 00:24:54,420
This guy's Bacchi's fucking delicious!

491
00:25:05,360 --> 00:25:08,242
This is one of the worst
drinks I've ever tasted.

492
00:25:09,640 --> 00:25:12,877
I think there may be something
wrong with your taste buds, kid.

493
00:25:12,960 --> 00:25:15,817
I think there's something
wrong with your big fat head.

494
00:25:15,900 --> 00:25:19,817
Well, I'm not the cook in this joint,
so I don't care what you have to say.

495
00:25:19,900 --> 00:25:20,730
Got it?

496
00:25:20,940 --> 00:25:23,780
Hey, Barkeep, I'll take 50 steaks to go.

497
00:25:24,100 --> 00:25:27,560
And I'll take 51 of those
delicious cherry pies to go.

498
00:25:27,700 --> 00:25:29,500
Wait, make that 52 steaks.

499
00:25:29,700 --> 00:25:31,397
Better make that 53 pie.

500
00:25:31,480 --> 00:25:32,800
Fifty-four steaks!

501
00:25:32,960 --> 00:25:34,060
Fifty-five pies!

502
00:25:34,340 --> 00:25:35,360
Sixty steaks!

503
00:25:35,520 --> 00:25:37,820
Seventy pies! Eighty! A hundred!

504
00:25:38,700 --> 00:25:40,737
I'm gonna beat the living crap out of you!

505
00:25:40,820 --> 00:25:43,097
Did you even have the slightest
idea what you're fighting about?

506
00:25:43,180 --> 00:25:44,945
Luffy, you promised, remember?

507
00:25:45,060 --> 00:25:47,817
Besides, we don't have enough
money to buy dozens of steaks.

508
00:25:47,900 --> 00:25:48,897
We aren't here to shop!

509
00:25:48,980 --> 00:25:51,660
Heh, so then, are you a pirate?

510
00:25:52,460 --> 00:25:53,578
Yeah, that's right.

511
00:25:53,840 --> 00:25:55,134
How big's your bounty?

512
00:25:55,640 --> 00:25:56,522
Thirty million.

513
00:25:57,540 --> 00:25:58,658
Uh, thirty million?

514
00:25:59,000 --> 00:25:59,830
For you?

515
00:26:00,120 --> 00:26:02,497
I wouldn't believe it
even if I collected it.

516
00:26:02,580 --> 00:26:04,837
Are you calling me a
liar, you fat, hairy ape?

517
00:26:04,920 --> 00:26:05,750
Enough!

518
00:26:05,880 --> 00:26:09,257
We've got rules in this place,
and one of them's no fighting.

519
00:26:09,340 --> 00:26:10,837
Here's your 50 cherry pies.

520
00:26:10,920 --> 00:26:12,580
Now please, just walk away.

521
00:26:31,600 --> 00:26:34,780
I'm looking for a pirate
that wears a Straw Hat.

522
00:26:36,780 --> 00:26:37,740
It's Bellamy.

523
00:26:42,960 --> 00:26:46,800
So you must be Straw Hat
Luffy worth a cool 30 million.

524
00:26:47,160 --> 00:26:48,120
Who's this guy?

525
00:26:48,360 --> 00:26:50,737
Looks like he has a bone
to pick with you, Luffy.

526
00:26:50,820 --> 00:26:54,097
That must be that Bellamy guy that
rented out the hotel we were at.

527
00:26:54,180 --> 00:26:55,037
Did you hear that?

528
00:26:55,120 --> 00:26:56,708
The kid's worth 30 million.

529
00:26:56,840 --> 00:26:57,680
No way.

530
00:26:58,420 --> 00:26:59,420
Tell me about it.

531
00:26:59,540 --> 00:27:02,337
How come everyone I meet
in this town is so tall?

532
00:27:02,420 --> 00:27:06,655
I'll take a glass from the top shelf
and give the kid whatever he wants.

533
00:27:07,540 --> 00:27:08,370
Right.

534
00:27:09,540 --> 00:27:10,660
Look at this place.

535
00:27:10,940 --> 00:27:12,580
This joint is packed solid.

536
00:27:13,460 --> 00:27:14,940
This place is disgusting.

537
00:27:15,160 --> 00:27:16,357
It smells like vomit.

538
00:27:16,440 --> 00:27:18,440
All you can get here is cheap rum.

539
00:27:18,560 --> 00:27:19,390
Look, Zoro.

540
00:27:19,473 --> 00:27:21,026
It's those guys from earlier.

541
00:27:22,980 --> 00:27:26,627
You'd be in a lot less pain if
you just offered us your seats.

542
00:27:26,820 --> 00:27:28,240
Pathetic harbor trash.

543
00:27:32,480 --> 00:27:34,820
It's him, Big Knife Sargus.

544
00:27:35,200 --> 00:27:38,141
How much you want to bet
he's looking for a fight?

545
00:27:38,420 --> 00:27:39,250
Oh, great.

546
00:27:39,980 --> 00:27:41,333
The whole gang is here.

547
00:27:41,440 --> 00:27:44,117
There's no way that they stopped
in just for a bite to eat.

548
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:45,030
Drop it, man.

549
00:27:45,113 --> 00:27:46,626
It has nothing to do with us.

550
00:27:46,940 --> 00:27:48,380
What's Bellamy up to?

551
00:27:48,860 --> 00:27:50,080
The usual fun.

552
00:27:52,280 --> 00:27:53,110
Cheers.

553
00:27:53,420 --> 00:27:54,977
Hey, thanks for the drink, pal.

554
00:27:55,060 --> 00:27:55,957
Well, you know what?

555
00:27:56,040 --> 00:27:57,040
You're all right!

556
00:28:06,720 --> 00:28:07,760
You did it!

557
00:28:10,360 --> 00:28:11,780
Brilliant move, Bellamy!

558
00:28:11,940 --> 00:28:12,822
Just brilliant!

559
00:28:16,660 --> 00:28:18,920
What are you doing, punk?

560
00:28:20,900 --> 00:28:23,841
That's the question you
should be asking yourself.

561
00:28:26,640 --> 00:28:28,300
Zoro! Don't do it!

562
00:28:28,420 --> 00:28:30,657
We still need to get some
information from - Quiet!

563
00:28:30,740 --> 00:28:33,328
This guy wants a fight,
I'll give it to him!

564
00:28:36,200 --> 00:28:38,318
So that's all you've got for backup?

565
00:28:42,040 --> 00:28:45,180
Now, are you ready to take me on or not?

566
00:28:46,720 --> 00:28:47,580
No way!

567
00:28:48,020 --> 00:28:49,902
The kid just challenged Bellamy!

568
00:28:51,580 --> 00:28:53,220
You'll be slaughtered!

569
00:28:55,060 --> 00:28:56,057
You've got it all wrong, kid.

570
00:28:56,140 --> 00:28:57,117
This isn't a fight.

571
00:28:57,200 --> 00:28:58,757
It's a test. Now, come on.

572
00:28:58,840 --> 00:29:00,546
Let's see how strong you are.

573
00:29:00,740 --> 00:29:01,900
Luffy, hold on.

574
00:29:02,400 --> 00:29:04,637
Mister, we're trying to
get to the Sky Island.

575
00:29:04,720 --> 00:29:06,602
Do you know anything about that?

576
00:29:11,080 --> 00:29:13,780
Did she just say Sky Island?

577
00:29:14,660 --> 00:29:15,540
She's crazy.

578
00:29:24,520 --> 00:29:27,932
Like I was saying, if you know
how to get to Sky Island...

579
00:29:33,840 --> 00:29:35,760
This is who I think is it!

580
00:29:37,560 --> 00:29:39,380
Sky Island, what an idiot!

581
00:29:39,900 --> 00:29:40,730
What the...

582
00:29:40,813 --> 00:29:42,774
You can look at the long pose yourself!

583
00:29:42,880 --> 00:29:45,115
It's pointed at the sky, plain as day!

584
00:29:48,400 --> 00:29:49,740
Hey, check it out!

585
00:29:49,900 --> 00:29:51,920
Do I look like the log foes now?

586
00:29:53,040 --> 00:29:54,997
No one trusts those things anymore.

587
00:29:55,080 --> 00:29:56,962
They break if you breathe wrong.

588
00:29:58,600 --> 00:30:00,120
You got me there, kid.

589
00:30:00,420 --> 00:30:02,577
I can't believe you guys
are putting open to such

590
00:30:02,660 --> 00:30:05,366
a ridiculous legend like
an island in the sky.

591
00:30:07,320 --> 00:30:09,517
Especially considering
how little you know.

592
00:30:09,600 --> 00:30:12,197
Like at the thousands of weird currents
cutting through the Grand Line,

593
00:30:12,280 --> 00:30:15,221
one of the weirdest is
called the knock-up stream.

594
00:30:15,940 --> 00:30:18,457
looks to me like this is
the first you've ever heard

595
00:30:18,540 --> 00:30:21,757
about it any ship that
gets caught in a knock-up

596
00:30:21,840 --> 00:30:24,997
stream is catapulted into
the sky and later slams back

597
00:30:25,080 --> 00:30:29,397
into the ocean years ago a
bunch of ignorant sailors saw

598
00:30:29,480 --> 00:30:32,237
ships falling from the sky
and assumed there must be

599
00:30:32,320 --> 00:30:35,237
an island up there somewhere
in their minds how else

600
00:30:35,320 --> 00:30:39,457
could a ship get up that
high ridiculous anything that

601
00:30:39,540 --> 00:30:42,517
seems supernatural always
has a rational explanation.

602
00:30:42,600 --> 00:30:45,129
Anything a man can
dream will eventually be

603
00:30:45,440 --> 00:30:47,597
explained and let me tell
you the truth will hurt.

604
00:30:47,680 --> 00:30:48,780
What a shame.

605
00:30:49,220 --> 00:30:51,400
Look, I was gonna let you join my

606
00:30:52,780 --> 00:30:56,877
crew if you'd pass the test of the new
era, but it seems like you're a lost cause.

607
00:30:56,960 --> 00:31:00,240
Thing is, the time of
pirates' dreams are over.

608
00:31:00,500 --> 00:31:04,088
The City of Gold, the Emerald
Ruins, and the Great One Piece.

609
00:31:04,220 --> 00:31:06,257
The fools who dream of
these fictional treasures

610
00:31:06,340 --> 00:31:08,597
don't notice the real
treasures that surround them.

611
00:31:08,680 --> 00:31:10,860
In this age of oceans,

612
00:31:11,180 --> 00:31:14,157
the very men who are brave enough
and capable of navigating currents

613
00:31:14,240 --> 00:31:17,887
end up chasing these ridiculous
dreams and die in the process.

614
00:31:18,460 --> 00:31:20,757
Whenever people speak
of these dead idiots,

615
00:31:20,840 --> 00:31:24,357
they always say he was happy
because he died living his dreams.

616
00:31:24,440 --> 00:31:25,270
Ha!

617
00:31:25,353 --> 00:31:27,260
No, he died because he was a fool.

618
00:31:27,820 --> 00:31:32,640
So when I see people chasing dreams
of One Piece, I get disgusted!

619
00:31:33,560 --> 00:31:34,390
Louie!

620
00:31:36,740 --> 00:31:39,357
You're a weak pirate, just like they were.

621
00:31:39,440 --> 00:31:42,537
And as long as you're hacking
around, you'll make us,

622
00:31:42,620 --> 00:31:44,620
the real pirates, look like trash!

623
00:31:47,300 --> 00:31:49,417
Get out of here, you scrawny punk.

624
00:31:49,500 --> 00:31:50,797
You're killing our bugs.

625
00:31:50,880 --> 00:31:52,160
Way to go, Bellamy.

626
00:31:57,700 --> 00:31:59,597
Bellamy, give these people what they want!

627
00:31:59,680 --> 00:32:00,780
Tear into them.

628
00:32:02,100 --> 00:32:04,280
I'd be more than happy to entertain.

629
00:32:06,740 --> 00:32:09,977
Luffy, Zoro, forget all that pacifist
crap I was talking about earlier.

630
00:32:10,060 --> 00:32:11,413
And take this jerk out.

631
00:32:12,380 --> 00:32:13,210
Zoro.

632
00:32:15,180 --> 00:32:17,800
No matter what happens, don't fight back.
